@[spell-options step]
The system you just installed was compiled with a particular set of spell
options: the answers to each spell's questions (e.g., which TLS library wget
uses, which locales are built) and which optional dependencies are enabled.
sorcery keeps using these answers whenever a spell is cast again, so it is
worth knowing what they are.

To list them for every spell that has any:
  @[enchantment options | less]
or for particular spells:
  @[enchantment options wget locale]

The same answers are stored in the installed system in
@[/etc/sorcery/local/depends/SPELL.p].

Nothing needs to be changed now. If you want a spell built differently, do it
after the install (or now, via @[enchantment chroot]) with:
  @[cast -r SPELL]
which asks the spell's questions again and recompiles it (this needs the
spell's sources, so usually network access).

When you are ready, type @[next].
